# M-package-manager step 2, panel 235's R1 and R18 (2026-11-07): a package's
# mark, `use <json>/parse`, and each habit beside it a model brings from
# another language, refused where the line is read with the message that
# names it. A repair is `certain` where the line it writes is the one meant
# whatever the catalogue holds: the whole path inside the brackets, a dot for
# the slash, a quoted name, the mark's parts apart. An address goes in the
# catalogue and never in a `use`, so its repair is a `guess`, the address's
# last part; a package with no module, an unclosed mark and an empty one have
# none.
use <json>/parse  #~ package_mark_holds_a_path
use <json>/text  #~ package_wants_a_slash
use <json>/lines  #~ package_name_quoted
use <json>/words  #~ package_mark_apart
use <json>  #~ package_wants_a_module
use <github.com/acme/yaml>/load  #~ use_holds_an_address
use <github.com/acme/yaml/dump>  #~ use_holds_an_address
use github.com/acme/toml/read  #~ use_holds_an_address
use <json  #~ package_mark_unclosed
use <>/x  #~ package_wants_a_name

function main()
    print(0)
